  "worked_solution": "We can calculate $\\frac{{x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}-4x-20}{x-2}$ using synthetic division.\n\nCarrying out the synthetic division process, we arrive at the following:\n\n|  | ${x}^{4}$ | ${x}^{3}$ | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2$ | $1$ | $2$ | $-1$ | $-4$ | $-20$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $2$ | $8$ | $14$ | $20$ |\n|  | $1$ | $4$ | $7$ | $10$ | $0$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}-4x-20}{x-2}={x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+7x+10.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
